---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

import steeringRewrapImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/steering-rewrap.png';
import processImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/process.jpg';
import pinkSteeringWheelImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/pink-steering-wheel.png';
import beforeAfterBmwImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/before-after-bmw.png';
import beforeAfterMercedesImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/before-after-mercedes.png';
import beforeAfterToyotaImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/before-after-toyota.png';
import alcantaraImage from '@/assets/steering-wheel/alcantara.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Custom Leather Steering Wheel Rewrap in Singapore | Five Star Auto Leather</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Worn or slippery steering wheel? Get a custom steering wheel leather wrap in Singapore for improved grip, comfort, and a refined finish. Book now!"
    />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-1">
      <Image
        src={steeringRewrapImage}
        alt="Porsche Boxster steering wheel finished with steering wheel leather rewrap service in Onyx black with contrast stitching"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[800]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center justify-center bg-black px-4 py-8 sm:order-2 sm:px-16">
      <div
        class="title-slide-up flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-center text-white sm:items-start sm:text-left"
      >
        <h1 class="text-4xl">Custom Leather Steering Wheel Rewrap in Singapore</h1>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Is your steering wheel worn, sticky or peeling? Five Star specialises in custom steering
          wheel rewraps using premium leather tailored to your vehicle. Restore grip and comfort
          with a factory-restored finish or custom look.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/contact-us"
          class="mt-8 inline-block w-36 rounded bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 text-center text-sm font-medium transition-colors hover:bg-red-600"
        >
          Get in Touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">Why Your Steering Wheel Needs a Rewrap</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Your steering wheel is the most frequently touched surface in your car. Over time, constant
        contact with sweat, skin oils, UV exposure and heat causes the original material to wear and
        deteriorate.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">Here are some of the most common signs:</p>
    </div>

    <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-gray-100">
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Common Sign</th>
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Why It Happens</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Shiny, slippery surface</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >The protective coating wears away, leaving the wheel smooth and reducing grip.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Peeling or flaking</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Common on leather-wrapped steering wheels as the outer layer ages and breaks down.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Sticky or tacky feel</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Often found in entry-level vehicles where the steering wheel is made from moulded
            rubber or polyurethane rather than wrapped in leather.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Fading or uneven colour</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Constant sun exposure causes the top of the steering wheel to fade faster than the
            areas that receive less sunlight.</td
          >
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-center">
      The good news? All these issues can be fixed with a steering wheel rewrap, giving you a fresh
      new look, better grip and a more comfortable drive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-6">
      <Image
        src={processImage}
        alt="Technician's hands dismantling a BMW M-series steering wheel during steering wheel rewrap service"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 lg:col-span-6 lg:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl lg:text-left">Our Steering Wheel Rewrap Process</h2>
      <p class="mb-8">
        See how a proper steering wheel rewrap comes together, from stripping the old material to
        the final hand-stitched finish inside our workshop.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 1: Free Assessment & Quote</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Bring your vehicle to our workshop or simply send us a photo of your steering wheel. As
        every wheel is different, we provide a tailored quotation based on its size, design and your
        chosen material.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 2: Safe Steering Wheel Removal</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We carefully remove the steering wheel so the airbag, horn, steering controls, paddle
        shifters and other electronic components are safely disconnected and handled with care.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 3: Surface Preparation</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The old worn material is carefully removed before the steering wheel is cleaned, smoothed
        and prepared for its new wrap. Any imperfections in the original wheel are addressed at this
        stage so the finish comes out clean.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 4: Handcrafted Leather Wrapping</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Your steering wheel is meticulously hand-wrapped using premium automotive upholstery
        materials. Every stitch is sewn by hand to achieve a precise fit, consistent finish and
        clean factory-style appearance.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 5: Reinstallation & Final Quality Check</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The completed steering wheel is reinstalled, with the airbag, steering controls and all
        electrical functions thoroughly tested. We also inspect the stitching, fitment, surface
        finish and overall feel before handing your vehicle back.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Typical turnaround:</strong> 4–5 hours for most vehicles.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="order-2 flex flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 lg:order-1 lg:col-span-6 lg:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl lg:text-left">Material Options</h2>
      <p class="mb-8 text-center lg:text-left">
        We offer a wide range of premium materials to suit your style, comfort and budget.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Premium Smooth-Grain Microfiber Leather</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        A clean, refined finish with a soft, luxurious feel. Durable, easy to maintain and an
        excellent choice for everyday driving.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Perforated Leather</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our most popular option. The perforated texture offers enhanced grip, improved breathability
        and excellent comfort, making it ideal for daily use.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Alcantara®</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        A premium suede-like material that delivers exceptional grip and a distinctive motorsport
        look. Perfect for performance-oriented drivers, though it requires a little more care to
        keep it looking its best.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Custom Colours & Stitching</h3>
      <p>
        Personalise your steering wheel with a wide selection of leather colours, contrast
        stitching, two-tone combinations and an optional 12 o'clock centre marker (GT stripe) for a
        sportier finish.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 lg:order-2 lg:col-span-6">
      <Image
        src={alcantaraImage}
        alt="Close-up of hand-stitched web pattern in blue and red thread on a custom leather wrap steering wheel"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured-2 h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <div class="text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl">Steering Wheel Types We Rewrap</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We can restore and rewrap virtually every style of steering wheel, including:
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="mx-auto space-y-2">
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span
            ><strong>Standard round wheels:</strong> the most common design found across all makes and
            models.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span
            ><strong>Flat-bottomed "D-shaped" or thicker grip wheels:</strong> a sporty look built for
            performance-oriented driving.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span
            ><strong>Multi-function wheels with integrated controls:</strong> buttons for audio, cruise
            control and hands-free functions are carefully reinstalled and fully preserved.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span
            ><strong>Wood or chrome trimmed wheels:</strong> the original wood or trim accents can be
            preserved, or fully wrapped for a completely refreshed appearance.</span
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-center">
        We work on all vehicle types, from Japanese and Korean makes to continental and luxury
        models, MPVs and commercial vans.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2">
    <Image
      src={pinkSteeringWheelImage}
      alt="Honda Fit two-tone custom leather wrap steering wheel in Peach pink and Onyx black"
      loading="lazy"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
      class="h-full w-full object-cover"
    />

    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 md:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl font-bold md:text-left">
        Why Choose Five Star Auto Leather?
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-8 text-center md:text-left">
        Choosing the right specialist for a steering wheel leather wrap in Singapore comes down to
        pricing, turnaround, materials and workmanship. Here is how Five Star Auto Leather delivers
        on all four.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Transparent Pricing</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Every steering wheel rewrap is quoted based on your wheel's design and your chosen material.
        No misleading "from" prices or hidden charges. Just fair, transparent pricing tailored to
        your vehicle.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Same-Day Turnaround, No Compromises</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Most steering wheel rewraps are completed within 4–5 hours. Throughout the process, the
        airbag, horn, paddle shifters, cruise control and multi-function steering controls are
        carefully removed, preserved and fully tested before handover.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Built for Singapore's Climate</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We use premium automotive upholstery materials that are heat and UV resistant, paired with
        high-performance adhesives where required. Designed to withstand Singapore's tropical
        climate, they're made to look and feel great for years to come.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">100% In-House Craftsmanship</h3>
      <p>
        Every steering wheel is rewrapped by our experienced craftsmen at our Singapore workshop —
        never outsourced. From preparation and hand stitching to final installation, we maintain
        complete quality control and back our work with a workmanship warranty for your peace of
        mind.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 pt-0 pb-8 sm:px-6 md:pt-8"
  >
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Before & After</h2>

    <div class="grid w-full gap-3 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <Image
        src={beforeAfterBmwImage}
        alt="BMW M4 steering wheel before and after steering wheel leather wrap Singapore service"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      />
      <Image
        src={beforeAfterMercedesImage}
        alt="Mercedes S320 steering wheel before and after steering wheel wrap service"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      />
      <Image
        src={beforeAfterToyotaImage}
        alt="Toyota Prius steering wheel before and after custom leather wrap steering wheel service"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-center text-2xl">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Do I need to remove the steering wheel myself?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          No. We take care of the entire process — from steering wheel removal and rewrapping to
          reinstallation and final testing. Simply bring your car to us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Will my airbag still work after the rewrap?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Yes. The airbag is carefully removed and reinstalled during the process. We do not modify
          or interfere with the airbag deployment system, and all functions are checked before your
          vehicle is returned.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Will the new dashboard match my original colour?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We aim to achieve the closest possible match using our extensive range of automotive
          upholstery materials and colours. While we cannot always guarantee an exact factory match,
          we can usually achieve a finish that closely resembles your original interior.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Will my steering wheel controls still work after the rewrap?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Absolutely. All multi-function buttons, paddle shifters, horn, cruise control, and
          steering wheel controls are carefully handled to ensure everything works as intended.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Can you make my steering wheel thicker?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Yes. If you prefer a chunkier grip, we can wrap over the existing steering wheel instead
          of removing the original covering (where suitable). This adds approximately 1.0-1.2 mm of
          material, giving the steering wheel a noticeably fuller feel.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">How long does a steering wheel wrap take?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Most steering wheel rewraps are completed within 4–5 hours, so you can usually have your
          vehicle back the same day.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Can I customise the design?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Yes. You can choose from a wide range of materials, colours, stitching styles and even
          centre markers. From retaining the original factory look to creating something completely
          unique, we'll tailor the steering wheel to your preferences.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <iframe
    src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3988.6660102489027!2d103.8690919!3d1.3770706000000001!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x31da1658b06d3b7d%3A0xbb4992fe537bc610!2sFive%20Star%20Auto%20Leather!5e0!3m2!1sen!2ssg!4v1766728446154!5m2!1sen!2ssg"
    width="100%"
    height="400"
    style="border:0;"
    allowfullscreen=""
    loading="lazy"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-family: 'RacingSansOne', var(--font-sans);
  }
</style>
